      "side": 1,
      "message": "After testing the fan in an Intrepid (based on constitution) device with `ectool pwmsetfanrpm` / `ectool pwmgetfanrpm all`, I found that the fan itself exhibits hysteresis: as we request it to spin faster, the actual fan speed is less than requested; as we request it to spin slower, the actual fan speed is higher than requested.  https://screenshot.googleplex.com/8fJaReQ5GMFAzjd\n\nDue to this hysteresis, I think the default `fan_percent_to_rpm` function will work just fine, and we should perhaps consider reverting the manually-specified fan tables in crrev.com/c/4060610.\n\nThe last time we changed the temp_fan_max was in crrev.com/c/4060610",
